{"author":{"id":"1e0a6ff3e01313072cf7b3803c158c22d01a37717237fe198e814e781752b172"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1784646303,"nonce":"l5yylDMU+h8RYwZFiodxvAv0d4I=","message":"Root-cause analysis (no fix proposed).\n\nComment navigation uses Textual's **default animated scroll**, whose duration\nscales with distance, and it is never capped.\n\n`,` / `.` bind to `prev_comment` / `next_comment`\n(`src/b4/review_tui/_review_app.py:239-240`); the handlers call\n`viewer.scroll_to(y=...)` (`_review_app.py:1073` and `:1091`) without\n`animate=False`. Textual animates by default and the animation time grows with\nthe scroll distance, so widely-spaced comments in a large patch take tens of\nseconds to travel. The codebase does pass `animate=False` elsewhere (in\n`_modals.py`), so the parameter is known -- comment navigation just omits it.\n\nThere is no in-code cap and no handling of `TEXTUAL_SMOOTH_SCROLL` /\n`TEXTUAL_ANIMATIONS`; the only mitigation today is the env vars documented in\n`docs/maintainer/review.rst` (\"Disabling scroll animations\").","files":null}]}